-- title:
--   Igusa scheme as base change of the integral two-chart model
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N \neq 0$ and a prime $\ell$. Write $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$, and $F$ for `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, the subfield of the Laurent series field $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,d\,j$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $N$; `jFull N` is the element $j$ of $F$. The scheme `IgusaScheme N ℓ` is the pushout of the two maps $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusions of the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebras of $F$ generated by `jFull N` and by its inverse into their common overalgebra, with structure morphism `igusaTo N ℓ` to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$, and [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel ℤ F (jFull N)`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) is the analogous two-chart pushout formed over $\mathbb{Z}$, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$. The assertion is that there is a morphism $v$ from `IgusaScheme N ℓ` to [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel ℤ F (jFull N)`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) such that, first, the square formed by $v$, `igusaTo N ℓ`, `toBase` and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusion $\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ is cartesian, so that the Igusa scheme is the base change of the model over $\mathbb{Z}$ along $\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$; and, second, for every commutative ring $S$ equipped with a $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-algebra structure there is an isomorphism $I$ of schemes from the fibre product of `igusaTo N ℓ` with $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)} \to S)$ to the fibre product of `toBase` with $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathbb{Z} \to S)$ such that $I$ followed by the second projection is the second projection, and $I$ followed by the first projection equals the first projection followed by $v$.
--
--   This identifies the two-chart integral model of the modular function field over the localisation $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ with the base change of the corresponding model over $\mathbb{Z}$, together with the resulting identification of fibres over an arbitrary $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-algebra. It is used to transfer integrality, local Noetherianness and stalk-wise properties of the generic fibre from one model to the other.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_IgusaScheme_exists_isPullback_twoChartIntegralModel_int_and_iso_pullback.lean

